    "cardQuote": "Yeah, this title is currently overadvertising the product... this seems to just stitch a \"push\" system to Postgrest for now (with no auth to boot).",
    "quote": "Yeah, this title is currently overadvertising the product. Without even getting into the non-OLTP DB parts of Firebase, Hasura is much further along towards being a Firebase replacement. It already handles auth and a basic admin UI for both the schema and data. I respect the vision and welcome more competition, but this seems to just stitch a \"push\" system to Postgrest for now (with no auth to boot).\n\nHasura also some limited support for generated multi-table transactional APIs, which Postgrest doesn't. Meanwhile, Firebase supports arbitrary read-modify-write transactions.\n\nThis team has its work cut out for them and I can see a fierce competition with Hasura and Firebase.",
    "storyTitle": "Supabase (YC S20) – An open source Firebase alternative",
    "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=23324061",
    "outcome": "4M+ developers. $5B valuation in 2025.",
    "outcomeDetail": "Supabase added auth, storage, edge functions, and a managed Postgres platform. By 2025 it had more than 4 million developers and a $5B valuation.",
    "note": "The launch build really was a realtime layer over PostgREST. Supabase closed the auth and platform gaps, then rode the AI-coding boom.",
    "sourceLabel": "Supabase press release",
